-- An untyped run initialises in source order (no checked order is carried), so `x`
-- reads `y` before `y` is initialised.  Both untyped drivers answer with an
-- internal-error panic naming `y`, never a silent value; the `expectedPanics` rows
-- in `test/diff_compiler_eval_test.mdk` pin it.
x = y + 1

y = 2

main = putStrLn (intToString x)
